# Game_Pacemaker — Virtual Pacer (ID 18)
# Files: src/coordinator/Game_Pacemaker.h, Game_Pacemaker.cpp
# HTML: data/game_pacemaker_setup.html, game_pacemaker_names.html, game_pacemaker_run.html

## GAMEPLAY
Virtual pacer game. Light moves along pucks at configurable pace. 1-2 groups follow the pacer.
Shuttle mode (back-and-forth) or linear mode. Two input modes: pace (min/km) or lap time.

## CONFIG
- inputMode: 0=pace (sec/km), 1=lap time
- paceSecondsPerKm (default 300 = 5:00/km)
- distanceBetweenPucks (meters, default 10)
- lapTimeMs (default 60s)
- durationMs (default 60s)
- shuttleMode, holdToStart, numGroups (1-2)

## STATES
PM_SETUP → PM_WAIT_HANDS → PM_COUNTDOWN (3s, SKI) → PM_RUNNING → PM_FINISHED
Optional: PM_FALSE_START (2s penalty)

## KEY MECHANICS
- msPerPuck calculated from pace/distance or lapTime/steps
- Shuttle: steps = (puckCount-1)*2, Linear: steps = puckCount
- Segment tracking: segment = elapsed / msPerPuck
- Halfway point detection: dims next-next puck, prevents audio stacking
- COUNTDOWN effect on current puck, speed = windowDuration / 35
- Two groups run independently with different colors (Green/Magenta)

## COMMANDS
setup, show_track, cfg_pace, cfg_dist, cfg_dur, cfg_shut, cfg_hold, cfg_inpt, cfg_lapt, cfg_grp,
change_pace, change_lap, start, stop, reset, exit

## STATUS JSON
{st, t (time remaining), lim, pace, dist, shut, hld, pucks, inpt, lapt, grp, run: [{h (holding)}], fs}
